  "known_gaps": {
    "no_opponent_tag_or_alive_capture": "red_tagged / red_alive are not read by _snap(). 'Home-side tags or protection metrics' (blue tagging red) cannot be measured; only red's CARRYING activity (whether red is holding blue's flag) is available as a defensive-benefit proxy.",
    "no_native_per_tick_score_event": "core's per-tick blue_cap_agents/red_cap_agents flags (the engine's own scoring-event signal) are internal to _step.py and not exposed. 'Time to score' is NOT computed. Instead, a carry-RUN is classified by how it ends, using only already-captured fields: ends while tagged or not-alive = 'tag-caught'; ends any other way = 'clean release' (a labelled PROXY for a likely capture, not the engine's own ground truth -- the macro vocabulary has no voluntary flag-drop action, so by elimination a clean release is either a score or the episode ending under the carrier, but it is reported as a proxy, not asserted as a score count).",
    "no_enemy_flag_position": "_snap() captures the OWN flag's position/home, not the enemy's, so no distance-to-enemy-flag 'progress' metric is computed. Offensive opportunity is measured by carry starts and carry timing only, not by spatial approach."
  },
